nd that  only happens every six years and so six  years ago on this Friday October 21st  Moonlight came out in theaters and so  six years ago to the day we were sitting  on a stage doing the same thing uh for a  different film and the 20 of you here  notwithstanding uh last night we were at  uh the AMC for like the public q a and  it was a sold out theater  um and we'll be again tonight and the  same thing at the Angelica in New York  and it's kind of cool to see that this  film moves at a very different Rhythm uh  than the films that are typically  filling the other 14 screens at a 16  screen Multiplex  um and yet there's an audience for this  Rhythm and I think just sitting at the  front of the stage and doing the Q a  with the Charlotte last night and  listening to seeing so many young people  bro I've seen so many young people  um sitting in the first few rows and  hopefully drinking in these images same  way they drink in the Avengers and  Ant-Man and all that stuff I think  there's something really wonderful about  that I think it just shows that you know  all the photos on the wall out there you  know of all those really amazing  filmmakers you know those same photos  apply to someone like Charlotte and a  story like this so yeah that's kind of  what I get out of it  thank you so much for being here the  three of you thank everyone for joining  us thank you thank you guys hey and if  you dug this fill let the 20 become the  40 become the 60 become the 120 tell a  friend tell a friend tell a friend  please thank you

